  "question": {
    "text": "Consider all rectangles lying in the region <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math> and having one side on the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis. The area of the rectangle which has the maximum perimeter among all such rectangles, is"
  },
